menu "Ito"

    config ITOFS_GEMM_FULL_SPLIT
        bool "Run the int8 GEMM on both cores (full split)"
        default n
        help
            Off (the default): the row split. Every GEMM call runs on core 0 and only the row-parallel loops (GELU,
            normalisation, depthwise convolutions, source features) use both cores. The output is bit-identical to the
            full split and the peak current is lower.

            On: the full split. Both cores run the GEMM. This is the fastest mode, but dense SIMD on both cores can
            collapse the 3.3 V rail of a board with a weak regulator or too little bulk capacitance, which shows up
            as hangs, brownout resets or wrong results. Enable it only on a board that passes the stress test in
            esp32/tools/stress (see esp32/DUAL_CORE_POWER.md).

            A compile definition S3_GEMM_DUAL_DEFAULT=0 or 1 (for example through ITOFS_EXTRA_DEFS) overrides this option.

endmenu
